
# Beyond Kubernetes: going serverless

This lecture is intended for seasoned devops people
who want to explore new ways of doing things on the
large commercial clouds in a way which makes kubernetes look like childs play. We will start with more down to earth examples and get to more high level examples.

I will show examples from both AWS and Google so as not to be biased towards AWS. I will not show examples from Azure simply because I know Azure less than the other two large commercial clouds.

## Here are the topics that we will discuss:
* AWS Lambda functions
* AWS API gateway
* AWS Elastic Beanstalk
* Google App Engine

The lecturer will be Mark Veltzer <mark.veltzer@gmail.com> who is a seasoned AWS instructor and certified professional architect on the AWS cloud and a seasoned Google cloud user.

The idea of the lecture is not to expose the participants to a specific feature of a specific cloud offering but rather to get a birds eye view of the more advanced options available and the road ahead for devops beyond Kubernetes.
